#{[{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502920 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "704c18d9-8ae5-5d2a-b5be-9c3bd783113a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}x^{4/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502916} {:answer/id #uuid "83c2bd22-9f4e-5d43-9304-91b91b9a28c5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}x^{-6/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502923} {:answer/id #uuid "bd03e86e-ee43-5358-9faf-d51843faec48" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{1}{5}x^{4/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502944} {:answer/id #uuid "cdbfdc00-4120-562c-9499-cddcd50a7e94" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}x^{-1/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502950} {:answer/id #uuid "f579062a-0b2f-501a-87d0-6b882f9a4596" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{4}x^{4/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502959}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "704c18d9-8ae5-5d2a-b5be-9c3bd783113a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{4}x^{4/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502916} :answer-field/id #uuid "0019a5a4-b1cd-503a-b7ea-8aa8c7427461" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502859}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "7466173d-cde9-509d-97b9-e88aaf8822fd" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)={x}^{-1/5}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{1}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-1/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/5+1}}{(-\\frac{1}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{4/5}}{\\left(\\frac{4}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5}{4}{x}^{4/5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502921 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "15d4daf1-ba4b-5a5a-9bfb-9fcfa0ec5e3f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-8/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502867} {:answer/id #uuid "16537613-9cc7-5cb0-93b0-7503cdac3395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-3/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502868} {:answer/id #uuid "3d2dd136-0894-52fa-aaf0-fb2dc0ac21a0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}x^{-13/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502894} {:answer/id #uuid "718ee9a6-017b-59f0-8c6e-948645ffc5f6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{8}{5}x^{-3/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502917} {:answer/id #uuid "ee7bf801-e0b2-5094-bcb2-972f291cbd49" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5}{3}x^{-3/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502958}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "16537613-9cc7-5cb0-93b0-7503cdac3395" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{5}{3}x^{-3/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502868} :answer-field/id #uuid "9de62160-8b1a-5cc7-89d0-103a6a2a4141" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502933}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "7db6e951-901a-5fa3-9344-ecedb4022de8" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{8/5}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{8/5}}={x}^{-8/5}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{8}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-8/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-8/5+1}}{(-\\frac{8}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-3/5}}{\\left(-\\frac{3}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3}{x}^{-3/5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{3{x}^{3/5}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502927 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "226b2f3f-2db8-5997-b937-8e623b198b43" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "5x^{-1/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502874} {:answer/id #uuid "343827b0-544c-50a0-9c05-84886ec4f608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x^{-1/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502885} {:answer/id #uuid "4235fe68-65b7-5e1e-8085-4b69c66d66c6" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x^{-6/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502902} {:answer/id #uuid "638899e9-e5e6-56ef-b39c-a5c6ac140c7b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}x^{-11/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502911} {:answer/id #uuid "f6be96f2-f588-5691-8f93-a2cb3d17caa1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{5}x^{-1/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502960}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "343827b0-544c-50a0-9c05-84886ec4f608" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-5x^{-1/5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502885} :answer-field/id #uuid "6f2d2ada-563b-5a0b-805f-7e51d4ac3934" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502915}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c4c3de5-5797-5a42-a678-da4fa4e6e5be" :question/problem "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{1}{{x}^{6/5}}$ and that ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x)$, calculate $F(x).$ Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Remember that integration is the opposite of differentiation. So, if ${F}^{'}(x)=f(x),$ then integrating both sides of this equation gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{F}^{'}(x) & =f(x) \\\\ \\int {F}^{'}(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\ F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that $\\frac{1}{{x}^{6/5}}={x}^{-6/5}.$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{6}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(x) & =\\int f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\int {x}^{-6/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-6/5+1}}{(-\\frac{6}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-1/5}}{\\left(-\\frac{1}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =-5{x}^{-1/5}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{5}{{x}^{1/5}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502931 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "17719d5d-d1ba-5a53-82a1-927b9ba2ae7a" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{6}x^{-7/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502869} {:answer/id #uuid "222ebe4e-7cc2-56b8-9528-6c4ba3801e4b" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{6}{7}x^{-7/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502873} {:answer/id #uuid "45cf63b0-27c9-5a38-89d8-9b07fe0e46ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}x^{-7/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502905} {:answer/id #uuid "e2c684a2-9fa1-565b-98df-fcb0427759b5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}x^{-13/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502956} {:answer/id #uuid "fb60838c-841d-5641-a911-df7407114bde" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{13}{6}x^{-19/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502962}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "45cf63b0-27c9-5a38-89d8-9b07fe0e46ca" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-\\frac{6}{7}x^{-7/6} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502905} :answer-field/id #uuid "9a8e6cf9-5e9d-5592-8b0f-70404484ce19" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502932}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "99719f66-3778-50b5-89e7-75e1a56079c8" :question/problem "Calculate the integral of $\\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{13}}}$. Assume $x>0$." :question/worked-solution "Note that $$\n\\displaystyle \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{13}}}=\\frac{1}{{x}^{13/6}}={x}^{-13/6}.\n$$ So, we can use the power rule with $n=-\\frac{13}{6}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\frac{1}{\\sqrt[6]{{x}^{13}}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{-13/6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{-13/6+1}}{-\\frac{13}{6}+1}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7}{x}^{-7/6}+C \\\\  & =-\\frac{6}{7{x}^{7/6}}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186502938 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "09fcd5be-886d-5871-98a0-3b7bbee18125" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "-6x^{-5} + C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186502864} {:answer/id 