:answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{5}}{5}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503865} {:answer/id #uuid "e85650a9-47ba-50b3-a4f1-3c07d1371853" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{3}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503872} {:answer/id #uuid "f079c239-840f-54f7-96fe-bbb4346258a9" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "x^{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503873}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "abbb6d1e-23ec-52ad-93a6-2a688bee49af" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{x^{4}}{4}+C" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503864} :answer-field/id #uuid "a740068d-6348-515e-8b5f-4399bec063f0" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503863}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "e2fcd99b-3b51-589f-9fd0-4c5df6da6a6c" :question/problem "Calculate $$\n\\displaystyle \\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$" :question/worked-solution "We apply the power rule with $n=3$, and we get\n\n$$\n\\int {x}^{3}\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{{x}^{3+1}}{3+1}+C=\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C.\n$$\n\nLet's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{4}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{4})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{1}{4}\\cdot 4{x}^{3} \\\\ &= {x}^{3}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503879 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "0d7829f8-6eb6-557a-9168-c1c357d9482c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503878}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "0d7829f8-6eb6-557a-9168-c1c357d9482c" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503878} :answer-field/id #uuid "1dad12b4-53d9-5ebb-9ae6-bd1949a26915" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503881}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "0f6eb79d-ca08-5993-aa8f-2308ed2df00b" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{5}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{5}}={x}^{5/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{5}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{5}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{5/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/2+1}}{(\\frac{5}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/2}}{\\left(\\frac{7}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{7/2}}{7}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{7}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{7/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{7}\\cdot \\frac{7}{2}{x}^{7/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{5/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503882 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b160a8b5-4564-5b27-8acf-8c7ae622a84f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503907}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b160a8b5-4564-5b27-8acf-8c7ae622a84f" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503907} :answer-field/id #uuid "9c8859ee-7542-5269-9360-31fde77bc9d0" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503899}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "2591c86e-cb60-5cb8-b4bb-3c4891ec69bc" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{3/2}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{3}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{3/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2+1}}{(\\frac{3}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/2}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{5/2}}{5}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{5/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{5}\\cdot \\frac{5}{2}{x}^{5/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{3/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503887 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "8e537889-fa35-53e7-a7d1-c9526c47ddf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503895}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "8e537889-fa35-53e7-a7d1-c9526c47ddf5" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503895} :answer-field/id #uuid "8523cfe1-fc1d-5cc8-b3ac-92d3c8d89541" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503892}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "5ebfc4c0-4a2d-5c2d-be2b-47c6ddfe06d1" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{1/2}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{1}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{1/2}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{1/2+1}}{(\\frac{1}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{3/2}}{\\left(\\frac{3}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{3/2}}{3}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{3/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{3}\\cdot \\frac{3}{2}{x}^{3/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{1/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503893 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "63820451-3b6f-5309-9075-931645a73f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503888}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "63820451-3b6f-5309-9075-931645a73f51" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503888} :answer-field/id #uuid "2abeee87-15e4-50b2-9c14-428aff34385c" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503884}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045487 :db/ident :question.difficulty/moderate} :question/id #uuid "8c4e1271-e72c-5666-b995-18dcd8b13de0" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}={x}^{9/2}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{9}{2}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[2]{{x}^{9}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{9/2}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{9/2+1}}{(\\frac{9}{2}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{11/2}}{\\left(\\frac{11}{2}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{2{x}^{11/2}}{11}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{11/2})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{2}{11}\\cdot \\frac{11}{2}{x}^{11/2-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{9/2}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503894 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b6ceeab1-a236-5548-8ed0-24d60c041807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503908}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "b6ceeab1-a236-5548-8ed0-24d60c041807" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503908} :answer-field/id #uuid "29a5b88e-4517-5fae-a7e6-afb8d22124ab" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503883}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045486 :db/ident :question.difficulty/hard} :question/id #uuid "8c582689-ffe0-5d18-bc8e-7ca7d9abd1e2" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We start by writing the root as a rational power, $\\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}={x}^{7/5}.$ So, we can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{7}{5}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int \\sqrt[5]{{x}^{7}}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\int {x}^{7/5}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{7/5+1}}{(\\frac{7}{5}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{12/5}}{\\left(\\frac{12}{5}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nAgain, let's check by differentiating:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}+C) &= \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}\\left(\\frac{5{x}^{12/5}}{12}\\right)+\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(C) \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{12}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{12/5})+0 \\\\ &= \\frac{5}{12}\\cdot \\frac{12}{5}{x}^{12/5-1} \\\\ &= {x}^{7/5}\\,✓\\end{aligned}\n$$"}] [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186503896 :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "a59f9be0-20c3-5247-aa01-a44a64642023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{5/3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503905}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "a59f9be0-20c3-5247-aa01-a44a64642023" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045498 :db/ident :answer.type/math} :answer/value "\\frac{3{x}^{5/3}}{5}" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503905} :answer-field/id #uuid "ba3c18ab-e570-5bd7-ba7b-e0fe86f89702" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045492 :db/ident :answer-field.type/blank} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186503909}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "9872673e-ba0e-5ee1-acfb-78f028930b51" :question/problem "Find the antiderivative of ${x}^{2/3}.$\n\nWork on $x>0$.\n\nThe antiderivative is {{field-1}} $+C$. Enter only the term before $+C$, with no additive constant." :question/worked-solution "We can apply the power rule with $n=\\frac{2}{3}$ and get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int {x}^{2/3}\\,\\text{d}x & =\\frac{{x}^{2/3+1}}{(\\frac{2}{3}+1)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{{x}^{5/3}}{\\left(\\frac{5}{3}\\right)}+C \\\\  & =\\frac{3{x}^{5/3}}{5}+C.\